                <pb facs="0429" n="321" xml:id="pg321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">704.5493/15: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-03-23T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 23,
                                1927—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 23—9:20
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>243. Department’s instruction 394, of December 31, 1926. Legation has ascertained
                    from French Legation that it is charged with protection of Swiss interests in
                    China. In view of this fact I respectfully request to be informed whether it
                    should act in accordance with the provisions of instruction aforementioned,
                    which I have deferred putting into effect pending receipt of information now
                    received, regarding the consular districts wherein Swiss nationals reside.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
